Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 01:17:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02224/11362] [outer-loop] E3 validated end-to-end on ar25:
 codex induces real model, verifier grounds it at 61%

Live codex/gpt-5.5 induced results/arc_e3/ar25/world_model.py -- a GENUINE world model
(flood-fill connected-component box dynamics, not a stub). Carnot WorldModelVerifier
scored it 73/120 = 61%, far above the 35% identity baseline -> codex captured real
dynamics and the verifier grounded it honestly. Planner correctly reports no in-model
win (the random transitions had 0 level-ups, so the goal predicate was unlearnable --
honest, expected). Fixes: bad to_logical import in plan_and_execute; --reuse flag
(re-verify/plan with zero codex). Full game-solve = the paper's multi-round refactor +
win-seeking loop (quota-gated conductor roadmap item). verifier_is_oracle=false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
